# Person-Average Scoring (Non-Negotiable)

## The rule

**Every number on this portal is a direct average of people. Nothing else.**

For any score, anywhere:

1. **Determine which people the number describes.** Org view with no filters is
   everyone in that campaign. Eighteen filters selected is the people who match
   all eighteen. A department bar is the people in that department. An index
   score is the same people, scored on that index's statements.
2. **Average those people directly.** Each person contributes one value — the
   mean of their own answers to the items in scope. Those person values are then
   averaged with equal weight.
3. **Never build a number out of other numbers.** No exceptions.

## Correct

```ts
personAverageScore(respondentsInScope, itemIdsInScope)
// per person: mean of their own answers to itemIdsInScope
// then: equal-weight mean of those person values
```

Scope is set by `itemIds` (one statement, one index's statements, or every
statement) and by the respondent population (campaign plus any active filters).

## Forbidden

- `mean(departments.map(d => d.score))` as org / Company Avg / vs Org
- `mean(visibleRows.map(r => r.value))` as a chart's average line
- `mean(index.statements.map(s => s.current))` as an index score
- `mean(indexes.map(i => i.score))` as an overall or Total Index score
- Averaging heatmap cells to produce a row average, column average, or grand total
- Pooling every respondent's raw answers into one flat list (that weights people
  by how many questions they answered — average each person first)
- Deriving a total from any level beneath it, on any perspective, ever

## How it is enforced in code

`ee-live-projections.ts` exports `personAverageScore` and precomputes person
averages so components never have to roll anything up:

- `index.score` and `projection.overall` — `{ byGroup, org }` `PersonScoreBlock`s
  for department, supervisor, location, division, job category, and brand
  projections. `org` is its own direct person average, not a roll-up of `byGroup`.
- `index.series` and `projection.overallSeries` — `PersonScoreSeries`
  (`byDept` / `byLocation` / `byOrg` per campaign) for the historical projection.
- `projectCampaignResultsData` — `index.score` and `overallScore`.
- `ComparisonHeatmap` requires `getColumnAverage`, `getRowAverage`, and
  `grandAverage` props; it will not average its own cells.

A single statement cell is already a person average of that one statement, so
statement rows may read those cells directly.

## When adding anything new

If a component needs an index, total, org, or segment score, read it from the
projection's person-average block. If the projection does not expose it yet, add
it there with `personAverageScore` — do not compute it in the component by
averaging what is already on screen.

Verify with `scripts/verify-person-average.mjs`, which recomputes every
projection independently from raw respondents and fails on any mismatch.

## Scope

Every current and future EE / assessment dashboard in this portal — DWS, Field,
CSG, and any client. Segment rows are person averages within the segment; org
and group rollups are their own direct person averages.
